<title>UK: Shell fails to fix VLCC Berge Nisa for U.S.</title>
<headline>Shell fails to fix VLCC Berge Nisa for U.S.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-06-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shell Transport and Trading said on Monday that it had failed to fix the Very Large Crude Carrier (VLCC) Berge Nisa for a trans-Atlantic trip loading mid-June.</p>
<p>&quot;We've failed that VLCC. It was too expensive,&quot; a trader at Shell's trading arm Stasco said.</p>
<p>Earlier, oil traders said Shell had fixed the vessel, adding that more players would be exploring arbitrage options after a Brent fetched a price of WTI minus 65 cents for early-July delivery into the U.S. Gulf on Friday.</p>
<p>--London newsroom, +44 171 542 8145</p>
